## Objective
- Continue bug bounty hunting for latest-version Naver Whale browser bugs in eligible scope (synchronization, Whale-only code, browser core on latest). Current phase: POC, target: sync encryption key derivation + bootstrap-token envelope storage.

## Important Details
- Eligible: latest-version Whale bugs (must reproduce on latest), third-party libs used ONLY by Whale (not Chromium), synchronization bugs.
- NOT eligible: Naver web services (*.naver.com, *.navercorp.com), built-in extension web servers (Papago/Belli), status-bar URL preview spoofing, XSS Auditor bypass, IETab, SafeBrowsing FP/FN ⇒ `api.whale.naver.com` sync backend is out of scope; only the client-side sync implementation is eligible.
- Passive-first only (≤1 rps, GET/HEAD); zero requests to Naver sync infra allowed; secrets in sha256 form only.
- Version context: latest desktop = v4.38.386.14; Android com.naver.whale 3.9.14.9 (vc 15965) SHA256 3c723291…, arm64 XAPK 166.29 MB; NVD: 21 Whale CVEs, 0 published in 2026 (6-month disclosure gap).
- Android binary mirror channels dead in sandbox: APKMirror/APKCombo/apk.support/apkpure → Cloudflare 403; uptodown → 410 Gone. Official desktop CDN `installer-whale.pstatic.net` WORKS and is now the acquisition path.

## Work State
### Completed
- Probed uptodown (`/android/download` and `/android`) → 410 Gone; apkpure.net → 403 Cloudflare. Android XAPK acquisition via mirrors is dead.
- Found official installer URL inside home2 JS bundle: `https://installer-whale.pstatic.net/downloads/installers/naver-whale-stable_amd64.deb` (from `https://shared-whale.pstatic.net/home2/assets/index-BFe9m_iX.js`).
